uè‹uŒàë… ÀQVø{{L–@"€Š†Û{"rendered":{"html":"<p>GCSL is a tree-walking interpreter with a typed intermediate\nrepresentation. The stages are separate so a formatter or editor can stop\nbefore execution while using the same syntax and type rules as the CLI.</p>\n<p>The main pipeline is:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\" data-language=\"text\"><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\" data-copy-code><span class=\"copy-label\">Copy</span></button><pre><code>SourceFile\n    -&gt; lexer and interned names/strings\n    -&gt; parser and arena-based syntax tree\n    -&gt; workspace resolution and type-check side tables\n    -&gt; type-specialized intermediate representation\n    -&gt; evaluation and a value with warnings\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The lexer and parser can recover enough structure to report multiple\nerrors. A failed check is never lowered into executable code. Recovery\nsupports diagnostics and editor queries; it does not make a partially\nvalid program executable.</p>\n<p>The checker resolves names and types expressions, recording captures,\nslots, argument destinations, and required awaits in side tables.\nLowering makes those awaits explicit. Evaluation dispatches through\nspecialized operations whose types have already been checked, rather than\nrepeating the type system at each operation.</p>\n<h2 id=\"pipeline--workspace-scheduling\"><span class=\"heading-number\">100.1</span> Workspace scheduling <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#pipeline--workspace-scheduling\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The workspace scanner merges public field paths, resolves imports, and\norders source files by dependencies. Each public leaf has an owner and a\ncell. Reading an interior record can require all its contributing owners.\nA cycle is a diagnostic, not an order selected at runtime.</p>\n<p>Top-level field scheduling differs from ordinary block order. It supports\nforward references while ensuring dependencies are initialized before a\nread. Shadowed declarations are still checked even when they do not\ncontribute a runtime value.</p>\n<h2 id=\"pipeline--sources\"><span class=\"heading-number\">100.2</span> Sources <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#pipeline--sources\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The principal implementation is in <code>crates/gcsl/src/lexer.rs</code>,\n<code>parser.rs</code>, <code>workspace.rs</code>, <code>check.rs</code>, <code>lower.rs</code>, and <code>eval.rs</code>.\nEach module documents its internal invariants. The implementation here is\nnot the separate Tree-sitter grammar used for highlighting.</p>\n","toc":[{"level":2,"id":"pipeline--workspace-scheduling","title":"Workspace scheduling","number":"100.1"},{"level":2,"id":"pipeline--sources","title":"Sources","number":"100.2"}],"has_mermaid":false,"dangling":[],"warnings":[],"broken":[]},"images":[],"links":{"pages":[],"anchors":[]},"refs":null}